WiFi Voucher API Documentation
1. Overview
The WiFi Voucher API allows merchants to issue, sell, and redeem prepaid WiFi vouchers from their allocated voucher inventory.
All WiFi Voucher API endpoints require the X-Merchant-ID header.
2. API Environments
Environment
Base URL
Production
https://kacyberpay.com

3. Authentication and Headers
All WiFi Voucher endpoints require the following headers:
Header
Description
Example
X-app-id
Application identifier
APP_TEST_001
X-API-Key
API authentication key
***************
X-Merchant-ID
Merchant identifier
M_TEST_001
Content-Type
Request content format
application/json

4. Available WiFi Vouchers
Endpoint
GET
/api/v1/wifi/vouchers/available
Description
Retrieves all available WiFi voucher products and the remaining voucher allocation for the merchant.
Request Headers
Header
Value
X-app-id
APP_TEST_001
X-API-Key
***************
X-Merchant-ID
M_TEST_001
Content-Type
application/json

Response
HTTP 200 - Successful Response
Field
Description
success
Request status
merchantID
Merchant identifier
products
List of available voucher products
productCode
Unique product identifier
name
Voucher package name
validity
Voucher duration
price
Voucher price
availableVouchers
Remaining voucher quantity
status
Product availability status

Sample Response
{
  "success": "true",
  "merchantID": "M_TEST_001",
  "products": [
    {
      "productCode": "WIFI_3H",
      "name": "3 Hour Pass",
      "validity": "3 hours",
      "price": "UGX 1000",
      "availableVouchers": 35,
      "status": "available"
    }
  ]
}
5. Purchase WiFi Voucher (KaCyber Collects Payment)
Endpoint
POST
/api/v1/wifi/vouchers/purchase
Description
Initiates a WiFi voucher purchase where KaCyber collects payment from the customer before issuing the voucher.
Request Body
Field
Type
Description
externalReferenceID
String
Merchant transaction reference
productCode
String
Voucher product code
msisdn
String
Customer mobile number
network
String
Customer mobile network
customerName
String
Customer name

Sample Request
{
  "externalReferenceID": "order-test-001",
  "productCode": "WIFI_3H",
  "msisdn": "+256700000001",
  "network": "MTN",
  "customerName": "Test Customer"
}
Response
HTTP 200 - Purchase Initiated
Field
Description
success
Request status
message
Transaction message
kacyberReference
KaCyber transaction reference
externalReferenceID
Merchant transaction reference
productCode
Purchased product
paymentReference
Payment transaction reference
amount
Voucher amount
status
Current transaction status

Sample Response
{
  "success": "true",
  "message": "Purchase initiated, awaiting payment",
  "kacyberReference": "KCYTEST001WIFI",
  "externalReferenceID": "order-test-001",
  "productCode": "WIFI_3H",
  "paymentReference": "PAYTEST001",
  "amount": "UGX 1000",
  "status": "pending_payment"
}
